{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards","id":1251560,"title":"Speculation: Dark Shards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-04T21:25:08-07:00","id":1251560,"title":"Speculation: Dark Shards","content":"So I saw somewhere that one of the upcoming things for Chronicles of Darkness will be called \u201cDark Shards\u201d. This gives me the impression of something like \u201cDark Eras\u201d, but with alternate settings instead of historical ones. If this is indeed what Dark Shards is going to be, what would you like to see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T21:35:24-07:00","id":1251561,"title":"","content":"We were told about one, 'Shattered Masks: A Shards (alternative) World Setting where the Masquerade comes down. What effect does this have on a world of darkness where vampires are suddenly real, and among us?' The Mirrors book, also, calls shards alternative worlds.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a fantasy Werewolf one, the game really fitting into it well. The standard mirrors tend to be post apocalypse, sci-fi, and fantasy, but they were already covered in the Mirrors books. It would be interesting to have one where, say, Pangaea didn't fall, the Gauntlet never came up and the dominance of predators was maintained, just as it would be interesting to see one where the moon, and thus Luna, no longer exist. Also I'm still hung up on Malcolm Sheppard's Father Wolf as Galactus/Nyarlathotep destroyer entity, with werewolves has his harbingers, decide whether to stick to the plan or fight against it seems like a nice idea for a shard.<br /> <br /> Also high school. For everyone. No idea how the vampires would do it, but that's always an entertaining prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T21:38:13-07:00","id":1251562,"title":"","content":"General setting, as opposed to splat specific?<ul><li> Infinite Macabre 2.0</li> <li> A real &quot;Fantasy&quot; Shard (Low, High, or both)</li> <li> Recursively, a Shard where each of the splats (and other phenomena) each occupy their own (private) copy of the world, connected by the God-Machine/Astral/whatever.</li> <li> A pulptastic superhero verse.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T21:40:28-07:00","id":1251563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1251561#post1251561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were told about one, 'Shattered Masks: A Shards (alternative) World Setting where the Masquerade comes down. What effect does this have on a world of darkness where vampires are suddenly real, and among us?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, as a follow on, on where monsters are celebraties. Or just fellow citizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T21:46:06-07:00","id":1251565,"title":"","content":"That have short comic where Narlythoptep, Cthulhu, Shub, and Yog form a rock band, but are on the verge of breaking up. Very strange, but also Cthulhu Mythos appropriate. So there would be a lot to mine in the premise of monsters as celebrities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T22:37:36-07:00","id":1251567,"title":"","content":"I suspect that they're probably going to be doing splat-specific settings for the most part, possibly with some two-or-three-splat crossover settings, and <i>maybe</i> with one or two Contagion-style general settings (since CC will be out by then, paving the way for all-splat crossovers). <br /> <br /> In that last vein, I'd like to see an updated version of the Woundgate setting from Mirrors. And speaking of Mirrors, maybe a Promethean/Geist post-Apocalyptic Shard? Prometheans are already pretty close to the survivor trope, and I could definitely see Sin-Eater society getting a massive population boost in the wake of an apocalyptic disaster. <br /> <br /> I'm also guessing that Dark Shards will minimize rules changes; and when they <i>do</i> change things, it will tend to be more cosmological (that is, changes to the world a la Woundgate) than personal (that is, changes relating to a splat, such as bringing back the Warg) \u2014 but that's just speculation; I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T22:46:14-07:00","id":1251570,"title":"","content":"How about a Bleeding Edge style Demon/Deviant Shard? From the Demon side of things, you'd have corporations as Infrastructure; from the Deviant side, you'd have the alienation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T03:08:46-07:00","id":1251597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1251567#post1251567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that last vein, I'd like to see an updated version of the Woundgate setting from Mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was premise of Woundgate setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T10:03:47-07:00","id":1251692,"title":"","content":"It's a modern fantasy Shard that adds hidden lands and cultures existing in the Shatter, a parallel reality that's separated from the regular world (a.k.a. the Corpse) by the Wound, and connected to it by Woundgates. The Shatter is very disjointed, and its inhabitants use the Corpse to get from one part of the Shatter to another. <br /> <br /> Realms within the Shatter include such places as the Wild Lakes (a Shatterland designed for sword and sorcery style fantasy, where modern technology fails and dragons roam the land), Undergotham (a series of small Shatterlands in New York City designed for more of an urban fantasy style), and Quivira-Cibola (a huge magitech city hidden in a Shatterland near New Orleans, designed for weird fantasy). Inhabitants of the Shatterlands include the same variety of beings that inhabit the Corpse (e.g., humans, vampires, werewolves, etc.), plus a few demihuman types such as Atlanteans, dhampirs, and Wargaz (inspired by, but distinct from, Mage, Vampire, and Werewolf, respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T14:29:11-07:00","id":1251759,"title":"","content":"I still try to process it... So Woundgate's Corpse works as our real world, only that all those smaller realities bleed into it, in various places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T17:07:01-07:00","id":1251790,"title":"","content":"Basically, yes; they're kind of like Terra Incognita in <b>Scion</b>: occult places existing just outside of regular geography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T06:24:37-07:00","id":1251899,"title":"","content":"I expect to see alternate template configurations. Of the &quot;what if the return ritual was done elsewhere?&quot; Interesting concepts that the gaming public wants, but that can not be added to the games soon we would have.<br /> <br /> - Inca and Chinese Mummies (&quot;What if the return ritual was done elsewhere?&quot;).<br /> - Werewolves associated with Covenants (&quot;And if the Heresies supplanted the war of Pure and Destitute?&quot;).<br /> &quot;What if the God-Machine was Mara?&quot; Or if Beyond the God-Machine there were the Christian Logos with their Angels and Demons?<br /> &quot;And if the Lords of Death were the Corruptor Gods of the Xibalba (for Geist).&quot;<br /> &quot;What if the Prometheans were the creation of supernatural models in the creative / servant struggle?&quot;<br /> &quot;And all the powers of the Magus derive only from his Watchtower, and they did not have access to the powers of the other towers?&quot;<br /> &quot;What if the Charlatans were the most common changelings?&quot;<br /> &quot;What if vampires extracted vitae from Breath and Will rather than Blood and had connection and government in some threshold realm?<br /> &quot;What if the Beasts were parasites coming from nightmares?&quot;<br /> - What if Deviants were created by Aliens and Horrors instead of Human Conspiracies?<br /> &quot;What if there were hunters chosen by some supernatural force?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T10:52:26-07:00","id":1251953,"title":"","content":"Some of these are already <i>there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T13:07:59-07:00","id":1251988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1251953#post1251953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these are already <i>there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very extremely, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T13:26:35-07:00","id":1251993,"title":"","content":"All the better. If something's already there, a Shard that features them is more a shift of emphasis than a change in the splat's basic nature \u2014 which IMHO is a good thing: Dark Shards shouldn't be about rules hacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:15:11-07:00","id":1252005,"title":"","content":"It's a book about scenario customization alternatives. Alternative versions of Templates are something much more usable in this respect than exotic alternative scenarios. In addition most basic changes still maintains the same atmosphere and creates elements for audacious tables have given a varied.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:18:08-07:00","id":1252006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1251993#post1251993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the better. If something's already there, a Shard that features them is more a shift of emphasis than a change in the splat's basic nature \u2014 which IMHO is a good thing: Dark Shards shouldn't be about rules hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they don't hurt either. \ud83d\ude1c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:51:29-07:00","id":1252016,"title":"","content":"Since it is my biggest sticking point on the list, allow me to ask then:<br /> <br /> How the fuck does doing Arisen style mummies in Incan or Chinese civilizations make a big enough difference to warrant a shard on it, and why would people want to play it.<br /> <br /> I'm not just interested in a &quot;people said so&quot; position, I want some actual exposure on the allure of the play space.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, on the rare off chance people forgot why this is a sticking point for me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=39949#post39949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mummy&quot; is not a generic archetypal monster even if the same term is used in English for a variety of preserved bodies. Having Incan mummies is a thematically incoherent addition to the game for the sake of a linguistic quirk. Mummy: The Curse is not about how it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-06-2018, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T19:21:54-07:00","id":1252081,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned this before in a media inspiration thread but since the prequel just came out it's rekindled my interest.<br /> <br /> In this series I'm reading, werewolves are sort of like vampires from Masquerade in that they can create their own werewolves and they all descend from one source. It seems easy enough to change Forsaken similarly. Father Wolf was the primogenitor, the Firstborn are its children, but werewolves instead of spirits, and falling down through the eons they get weaker in power the farther away they get from the source, though always maintaining some basic werewolf abilities and vulnerabilities while upping their territorial and dominant instincts and their magicness (hey immortality). Just the way I see it, it would make things a much more personal game, like for smaller groups of one to three players, simply because a pack of more than that would be really difficult to hold together. Totems and Luna would seem to be out, and you wouldn't have the divide between the Pure and Forsaken, though you would have animosity between Lineages that didn't get along due to feuds among their ancestors. Wolf-blooded would be the same with their Tells upped a bit (in the drawback and power side), spawned only from the werewolves and there's a tendency to avoid turning them into werewolves as you get mixed results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T05:16:40-07:00","id":1252184,"title":"","content":"I feel like the &quot;What if the masquerade came down&quot; shard would be cool, but I would like to see a variant &quot;What I'd the masquerade never went up!&quot; The premise is everyone has always known about the supernatural and it has integrated into the world completely. <br /> Especially I would like to see what if the God-Machine had been a known companion to humanity the whole time. Would there be churches as big as Christianity for it? <br /> How would countries look to resist?<br /> What do Mage's, werewolves and vampire's think about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":24597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","user":"LordofIron","date":". 09-07-2018, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T09:51:30-07:00","id":1252253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252081#post1252081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've mentioned this before in a media inspiration thread but since the prequel just came out it's rekindled my interest.<br /> <br /> In this series I'm reading, werewolves are sort of like vampires from Masquerade in that they can create their own werewolves and they all descend from one source. It seems easy enough to change Forsaken similarly. Father Wolf was the primogenitor, the Firstborn are its children, but werewolves instead of spirits, and falling down through the eons they get weaker in power the farther away they get from the source, though always maintaining some basic werewolf abilities and vulnerabilities while upping their territorial and dominant instincts and their magicness (hey immortality). Just the way I see it, it would make things a much more personal game, like for smaller groups of one to three players, simply because a pack of more than that would be really difficult to hold together. Totems and Luna would seem to be out, and you wouldn't have the divide between the Pure and Forsaken, though you would have animosity between Lineages that didn't get along due to feuds among their ancestors. Wolf-blooded would be the same with their Tells upped a bit (in the drawback and power side), spawned only from the werewolves and there's a tendency to avoid turning them into werewolves as you get mixed results.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The choice of a lycanthropic tribe (in the sense of disease transmission) sounds more interesting to me, than all of them are like that.<br /> <br /> But if I have to choose I prefer the adaptation of the Covenants system, so that the Tribe is the wolf ideology and the Human Covenant about the condition and the tribes gain archetypal aspects. You are born into the tribe and choose the covenant and have a sign about when it has become.<br /> <br /> But I think we can have both.<br /> <br /> <br /> ___________________________________<br /> <br /> About Mummies as Latino I have an interest in representing the cultures of our people in games. But it seems there is a certain prejudice here against this type of representation, the point of the mask for example to defend the survival of the Egyptian culture and its integration into Greek, but not the survival of Aztec culture and its integration into the Spanish in Mexico (because a coherent scenario the Sabbat would have three cultural forces, the Aztec being one next to the Lasombra Christianity and the Tzimisce paganism).<br /> <br /> Here at pains seems to be the same, there is no mention of the Andean ritual of Mummification and treats them as just natural phenomena, although I understand that on the Andean exists little material in English, you do not have the data to Inca writing beyond quipus to contrary to the studies of Rafael Larco Hoyle. The same happens with the funeral rites described by Roel Pineda.<br /> <br /> Here we know that the Mummies were made up of people of the Nobility who after being sacrificed went through specific funeral rites that use sacred salt to represent the community while taking part with the Gods and being able to intermediate the end of droughts. They are associated with water powers. And their residences were sacred and terrible Huacas. The sacrifices were elevation and non-commensalism with the Gods in balance as in the Aztecs and therefore much more unusual (we also do not have the concept of many deaths and death before life, further follows the Western pattern of life followed by death in a line, though the gods are transmuted and the unborn are underground that in Inca cosmology is always mistaken for water). The Tawantinsuyans (who were not priests but were not &quot;academics&quot; and &quot;philosophers&quot; as the Old World or Meso-Americans - actually resembled teachers and sophists before Socrates changed the function of Greek thought) also proposed the thesis of that we have 5 souls in a system similar to Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:24:26-07:00","id":1252262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252253#post1252253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here we know that the Mummies were made up of people of the Nobility who after being sacrificed went through specific funeral rites that use sacred salt to represent the community while taking part with the Gods and being able to intermediate the end of droughts. They are associated with water powers. And their residences were sacred and terrible Huacas. The sacrifices were elevation and non-commensalism with the Gods in balance as in the Aztecs and therefore much more unusual (we also do not have the concept of many deaths and death before life, further follows the Western pattern of life followed by death in a line, though the gods are transmuted and the unborn are underground that in Inca cosmology is always mistaken for water). The Tawantinsuyans (who were not priests but were not &quot;academics&quot; and &quot;philosophers&quot; as the Old World or Meso-Americans - actually resembled teachers and sophists before Socrates changed the function of Greek thought) also proposed the thesis of that we have 5 souls in a system similar to Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Write it out more? The current antipathy seems to be derived from people want Arisen from other cultures where the similarity is extremely shallow (see: the word Mummy is used, but being a preserved corpse is the extent of the linkage). If there <i>are</i> deeper similarities, please point them out.<br /> <br /> The Curse's mechanics and corresponding backstory still heavily favor a particular model, but it many not be as exclusive as previously thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:02:00-07:00","id":1252284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252253#post1252253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I have to choose I prefer the adaptation of the Covenants system, so that the Tribe is the wolf ideology and the Human Covenant about the condition and the tribes gain archetypal aspects. You are born into the tribe and choose the covenant and have a sign about when it has become.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by covenants. The tribes in Forsaken are like covenants. You aren't born into tribes in Forsaken, you choose to join one because their method of dealing with being with the Uratha appeals fits your own ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T20:19:03-07:00","id":1252427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252284#post1252284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you mean by covenants. The tribes in Forsaken are like covenants. You aren't born into tribes in Forsaken, you choose to join one because their method of dealing with being with the Uratha appeals fits your own ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But shifting the tribe to something that &quot;you are born&quot; rather than &quot;you swear&quot; does not lose all concept, tradition and culture. Still the same thing.<br /> <br /> The &quot;covenants&quot; would occupy the position of the Pure and Destitute, as sects. In the case he would use the Heresies as mentalities of the devotion legends of what created them and what work the werewolves as a whole must have, again replacing the pure and destitute.<br /> <br /> I like Shard because he only needs a small introductory text, five small sects texts and 5 lists with 5 gifts in each. It is the shortest material possible, you can have this fully functional Shard with 4 pages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T22:31:08-07:00","id":1252443,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong: I have no problem with rules hacks; check my sig for an idea of how much I love them. But I'd rather see them in the various gamelines' Storyteller Guides, the way the Demon Storyteller's Guide included system hacks. Dark Shards shouldn't be about system hacks; it should be about alternate settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T22:46:35-07:00","id":1252445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252184#post1252184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the &quot;What if the masquerade came down&quot; shard would be cool,</div> </div> </div> </div>...you mean the one that's already getting its own book?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Shattered Masks:</b> A Shard where the Masquerade comes down. What effect does this have on a world of darkness where vampires are suddenly real, and among us? <i>PDF/PoD</i></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252253#post1252253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Mummies as Latino I have an interest in representing the cultures of our people in games. But it seems there is a certain prejudice here against this type of representation, the point of the mask for example to defend the survival of the Egyptian culture and its integration into Greek, but not the survival of Aztec culture and its integration into the Spanish in Mexico (because a coherent scenario the Sabbat would have three cultural forces, the Aztec being one next to the Lasombra Christianity and the Tzimisce paganism).</div> </div> </div> </div>To which I'd ask:<br /> <br /> Why Mummy specifically? What's wrong with using one of the other gamelines as a means to spotlight and often-overlooked region and culture to the Western world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T00:48:23-07:00","id":1252454,"title":"","content":"Eh. As much as I disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> about putting Andean mummies into Dark Shards, \u201cwhy mummies, specifically, and not something else?\u201d is easily addressed: first, it's not an either/or decision. You can do Andean mummies <i>and</i> something with other gamelines to spotlight South American culture. Heck, if they wanted to, Onyx Path could do something similar to old White Wolf's Years of the Lotus and the Scarab (which focused on the Far East and Egypt respectively) with every gameline contributing something to the effort. I don't think they're <i>going</i> to; but it's not an impossibility. <br /> <br /> So that addresses the \u201cwhy not focus on another gameline <i>instead</i>?\u201d issue. The other issue is \u201cWhy mummy?\u201d There are actually very few cultures in history that actively practiced mummification; and one of the things they all had in common was a belief in some sort of life after death. Despite Malcolm's rather flippant answer, <i>that</i>, moreso than the practice of preserving corpses itself, is what draws people to a game about those other cultures. We've already got a pseudo-Egyptian take on things with the Arisen; why <i>not</i> address the others? <br /> <br /> Now, I'm not suggesting that OP provide a hack that reskins the Arisen as Andean or Chinese mummies. <i>That</i>, in my view, would be lazy and derivative. But bear in mind that the Chronicles of Darkness already have at least three distinct kinds of entities called \u201cdemons\u201d \u2014 and I'm not talking about the wide variety of entities that could broadly be described as \u201cdemonic\u201d; I'm talking about creatures that are directly and explicitly called \u201cdemons\u201d. There are the Unchained rebels against the God-Machine; the Infernal demons intruding on our reality in search of Vice; and the Supernal denizens of Pandemonium who seek to run people through an iron gauntlet of temptations to see who survives and thrives. There may be more. <b>Wicked Dead</b> explicitly brought us vampires who aren't Kindred, after <b>Night Stalkers</b> had implied their existence. <b>Skinchangers</b> (and, more controversially, <b>Changing Breeds</b>) brought us other shapeshifters, including other kinds of werewolves \u2014 something that was hinted at in <b>Spirit Stalkers</b>. There are also several kinds of magic wielders in the Chronicles of Darkness that aren't the Awakened. <br /> <br /> Ahem; sorry for that tangent. My point is that there's a rich tradition of alternatives to the main splats of what has become the Chronicles of Darkness; indeed, \u201cThere are more things in Heaven and on Earth than are dreamt of in your philosophy\u201d doesn't just apply to the rational Horatio in the Chronicles of Darkness; it applies to <i>everyone</i>. I don't see why you can't have alternate takes on life-after-death immortals, i.e., mummies. Heck, we already <i>have</i> one: the Purified, from <b>Immortals</b>. If the Purified get reintroduced into the Chronicles of Darkness by way of <b>Mummy</b>, it wouldn't hurt to have the first Arisen to leave the Middle East encounter Purified immortals spreading throughout the Far East, cementing them as the kind of immortals descended (figuratively) from a proto-Chinese culture in a vaguely similar way to how the Arisen are descended from a proto-Egyptian culture. Their power stat, after all, is \u201cChi\u201d; and I've heard them described loosely as \u201cmonks and alchemists\u201d \u2014 there's a lot about them that could be cast as having originated in China, though they have (by now) long since grown past that as the secret of Purification has spread to other cultures.<br /> <br /> I could also definitely see Andean mummies being a thing. It's just that I'd want to see them be <i>their own thing</i> not just copycats of the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Elaborated further on the Purified 09-08-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T10:17:19-07:00","id":1263211,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see, but don't expect to, would be a \u201cTime Before\u201d Shard for <b>Mage</b>: what was it like before mages needed Watchtowers to Awaken to one of five Paths, and there was no Sleeping Curse forcing mages to hide their magics from the public?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:36:24-07:00","id":1263228,"title":"","content":"On the topic of foreign mummies, wasn\u2019t that brought up in panel during Gen Con? Like while every mummy will keep its origin as Irem, but because of the changes they are making in the perspectives that mummies expierence between Descents you can have a mummy\u2019s first time awakening be in the deep of ancient China and starting their expierence from there?<br /> <br /> Also the Purified is definitely getting reintroduced in Mummy, they said that pretty much explicitly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:41:50-07:00","id":1263230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263228#post1263228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of foreign mummies, wasn\u2019t that brought up in panel during Gen Con? Like while every mummy will keep its origin as Irem, but because of the changes they are making in the perspectives that mummies expierence between Descents you can have a mummy\u2019s first time awakening be in the deep of ancient China and starting their expierence from there?<br /> <br /> Also the Purified is definitely getting reintroduced in Mummy, they said that pretty much explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first point was present in the first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:50:16-07:00","id":1263232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263228#post1263228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of foreign mummies, wasn\u2019t that brought up in panel during Gen Con? Like while every mummy will keep its origin as Irem, but because of the changes they are making in the perspectives that mummies expierence between Descents you can have a mummy\u2019s first time awakening be in the deep of ancient China and starting their expierence from there?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's always been the case. I could definitely see it getting more emphasis on 2e; though that doesn't really address the concerns of those who want Andean mummies (as opposed to Egyptian mummies that migrated to the Andes). But as I said above, I think the matter could easily be addressed by giving us Andean mummies that are as different from the Arisen as the Purified are. Speaking of which:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263228#post1263228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Purified is definitely getting reintroduced in Mummy, they said that pretty much explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! Did they say anything else? Given <b>Mummy</b>'s focus on history, Is love to see the Purified get some more history of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:55:27-07:00","id":1263233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263232#post1263232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great! Did they say anything else? Given <b>Mummy</b>'s focus on history, Is love to see the Purified get some more history of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>We\u2019re getting all of the immortals from the book into Mummy 2e. They will fill the role of Rank 3 Cultists if the become beholden under the mummy, which is just under a Sadikh, which would be Rank 4. The rank the cultist has determines how much Pillars a mummy can infuse them with to empower them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T12:57:39-07:00","id":1263234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263230#post1263230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first point was present in the first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but with how a Mummies expierence is none linear I can see that playing much more of a role then it did before","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:04:20-07:00","id":1263235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252016#post1252016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the fuck does doing Arisen style mummies in Incan or Chinese civilizations make a big enough difference to warrant a shard on it, and why would people want to play it.<br /> ...<br /> EDIT: Also, on the rare off chance people forgot why this is a sticking point for me</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>not</i> weird that English uses the same word for different instances of preserved bodies. We don't have different words for skeleton based on how and why the flesh was removed.<br /> <br /> That &quot;why&quot; brings me to why I'm interested in the idea of Andean (not specifically Inka) mummies, which is that many of the concepts surrounding the Deathless - acting as messengers between the earthly and divine, being worshipped by related communities, an expectation that they might continue to act in the world - actually fit them rather well, better than Egyptian ones. Not all the time, and not all at once - different Andean cultures mummified people for different reasons, and sometimes it was just a funerary practice. But it also makes Mummy the game with the tools already there to represent them.<br /> <br /> And what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1251562#post1251562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General setting, as opposed to splat specific?<ul><li> Infinite Macabre 2.0</li> <li> A real &quot;Fantasy&quot; Shard (Low, High, or both)</li> <li> Recursively, a Shard where each of the splats (and other phenomena) each occupy their own (private) copy of the world, connected by the God-Machine/Astral/whatever.</li> <li> A pulptastic superhero verse.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>They all sound viable. But I'd prefer the last of those to mimic the original pulps more than pulp RPG's - that is the originals only used a few &quot;pulp things&quot; at a time rather than throwing everything into the mix. Make it more like The Shadow than Jet-Pack Apes from Mars vs the Hollow Earth Vampires. Or maybe one for each.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1252454#post1252454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also definitely see Andean mummies being a thing. It's just that I'd want to see them be <i>their own thing</i> not just copycats of the Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my daydreams for Onyx Path is short &quot;lines&quot; focussed on great regions rather than species. A core book of advice on creating mortal characters from the cultural blocs of the region, and supplements of similar advice for the supernatural lines, plus a book giving a full treatment to a new type of supernatural. But anyway, that's not about dark shards.<br /> <br /> <br /> One idea might be Shards based mixing up the games' different moods. Like, what if werewolves were as socially shapeshifting as they are physically and werewolf society had the ad-hoc trash culture vibe of the Geist? What if Beasts are more like werewolves, dedicated to maintaining a balance between the astral and the mortal? What of demons were free from the threat of the God-Machine, and able to build up their Hells - or sabotage each other's - would they live more like vampires or mages? How would it change mage society if they *had* to get mana from harming humans, making them obligate parasites/predators like vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:22:50-07:00","id":1263238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263235#post1263235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>not</i> weird that English uses the same word for different instances of preserved bodies. We don't have different words for skeleton based on how and why the flesh was removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a skeleton becomes a thing that vertebrates don't have by default as a matter of course with no special required circumstance, this will be an argument you can make with any relation to the argument that the Arisen variety of mummy needs a Shard based purely on the Rite of Return being carried out in a different part of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:28:40-07:00","id":1263239,"title":"","content":"On a Shard idea I think would be cool that opens up with the Shattered Masquerade bit, a completely open supernatural society, where the supernatural not only in open as a normal thing but in fact essential with workings of said society. Basically this is based on a setting idea I've been fuming for a bit which is a little inspired by anime like <i>Kekkai Sensen</i><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, and some other fantasy works. In that a city was founded by various factions of all splats who came together for various sorts of reasons, whether as a desire to escape from enemies or wishes to create a place they wouldn't have to be hunted thus deciding on creating and hiding a society </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">through various and powerful magics with all of them cooperating for each other where the others were lacking. Well that is at least something I want to see on homebrewing and possibly putting on the ST vault. Though for now I'm just putting that idea on hold until Contagion Chronicle comes out since I want to use that as a plot device to open the city to outsiders.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anyhow though so an idea of the supernatural splats being in the open as mundane things interests me, though I would not just want to see them just being seen as mundane but on what effect their supernatural abilities would have on influencing and changing a society and how that would work when you have people being able to do said things in the open.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:47:04-07:00","id":1263246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263238#post1263238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a skeleton becomes a thing that vertebrates don't have by default as a matter of course with no special required circumstance, this will be an argument you can make with any relation to the argument that the Arisen variety of mummy needs a Shard based purely on the Rite of Return being carried out in a different part of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's an argument I can make in relation to that glib soundyte. My argument about the Shard was something else, a whole different paragraph and everything - which if you read it more carefully, didn't include me saying I wanted one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:48:02-07:00","id":1263247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263234#post1263234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but with how a Mummies expierence is none linear I can see that playing much more of a role then it did before</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely depends on how it plays out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:51:37-07:00","id":1263248,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's a possible Shard for Mummy: what if human society knows that Irem existed (ruins are known, there are mentions of it in Egypt and Kush, and maybe Saba or Axum), but does <i>not</i> know about the Deathless? How much would that change, do you think?<br /> <br /> And a crossover one. Imagine a fully integrated set of myths: the God Machine is the same as the Exarchs, one Arcadia, the Underworld and Hisil abutting Stygia and Pandemonium (or the Primal Wild depending on how you see the Hisil) the way the Hedge does Arcadia, the Strix realm/Inferno/Principle/Duat being anti-Supernal Realms, the Crone = the Dark Mother = Mother Moon and so on.<br /> The point is not whether it's true (it doesn't have to be) - the point is that almost supernaturals believe it to be true, and how this affects their socities and interrelations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 10-28-2018, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:56:02-07:00","id":1263250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263246#post1263246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's an argument I can make in relation to that glib soundyte. My argument about the Shard was something else, a whole different paragraph and everything - which if you read it more carefully, didn't include me saying I wanted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing of the matter is that it's not a glib soundbyte, and I'll thank you to not treat it as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:04:29-07:00","id":1263252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263250#post1263250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing of the matter is that it's not a glib soundbyte, and I'll thank you to not treat it as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will call it as I see it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:16:21-07:00","id":1263254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263246#post1263246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's an argument I can make in relation to that glib soundyte. My argument about the Shard was something else, a whole different paragraph and everything - which if you read it more carefully, didn't include me saying I wanted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ability to read works just fine. The quote you were replying to was addressing a point that has nothing to do with what you want.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263252#post1263252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will call it as I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to get your eyes fixed so you don't make replies to &quot;glib soundbytes&quot; from two months ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T16:01:05-07:00","id":1263275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263246#post1263246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's an argument I can make in relation to that glib soundyte. My argument about the Shard was something else, a whole different paragraph and everything - which if you read it more carefully, didn't include me saying I wanted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about this is that Mummy the Curse so clearly steeped into a Gothic re-imagining of <i>explictly</i> <i>Egyptian mummy mythos and folklore</i> that it doesn't actually map well to other cultures in the same sort of way.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Hack&quot; or &quot;Shard&quot; of Mummy the Curse for Andean, Chinese, or other cultural body is not so much a hack or shard as it is <i>whole new gameline</i>. It's like trying to take the humanism out of Promethean-at some point, you're better served by just going to another game.<br /> <br /> You want to do immortals that relate to those cultures preserved bodies, I'm up for that idea in Chronicles-but Mummy the Curse is not the game you go to for that just because it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T18:15:10-07:00","id":1263288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263275#post1263275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;Hack&quot; or &quot;Shard&quot; of Mummy the Curse for Andean, Chinese, or other cultural body is not so much a hack or shard as it is <i>whole new gameline</i>. It's like trying to take the humanism out of Promethean-at some point, you're better served by just going to another game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes! This! You've got it dead on! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263275#post1263275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want to do immortals that relate to those cultures preserved bodies, I'm up for that idea in Chronicles-but Mummy the Curse is not the game you go to for that just because it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026save only for the fact that it's <i>not</i> weird that English uses the same word for preserved corpses, regardless of the details. There are <i>lots</i> of cases where English uses one word to describe a disparate collection of things that only have one property in common. In this case, that property is pretty close to \u201cpreserved corpses\u201d. What's so weird about that? <br /> <br /> All of which has nothing to do with your main point (that Andean mummies should be something different from Egyptian mummies), which I agree with. It's just that \u201cmummy means \u2018preserved corpse\u2019\u201d isn't the slam-dunk argument in favor of that point that you seem to think it is. <br /> <br /> In other news, I'm now worried: I <i>like</i> the fact that the Purified aren't specifically Egyptian in nature, and if anything lean a bit more closely toward Chinese culture and mythology; and I'm worried that recasting them primarily as cultists for the Arisen will cost them that distinction. It's the problem of the game being fundamentally tied to (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts: the closer something else gets tied to the game, the closer it also gets tied to the same (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts, if only by proximity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T19:32:58-07:00","id":1263295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263288#post1263288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes! This! You've got it dead on! <br /> <br /> \u2026save only for the fact that it's <i>not</i> weird that English uses the same word for preserved corpses, regardless of the details. There are <i>lots</i> of cases where English uses one word to describe a disparate collection of things that only have one property in common.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Vampires, or Gods<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In other news, I'm now worried: I <i>like</i> the fact that the Purified aren't specifically Egyptian in nature, and if anything lean a bit more closely toward Chinese culture and mythology; and I'm worried that recasting them primarily as cultists for the Arisen will cost them that distinction. It's the problem of the game being fundamentally tied to (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts: the closer something else gets tied to the game, the closer it also gets tied to the same (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts, if only by proximity. </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think so, other then mabye Sadihk all the other Cultists are all from the various cultures that the Mummie interacts with and pulls to worship him. As why Immortals would worship the Arisen is less to do with being of the cultural theme but they consider the Arisen to be perfect Immortals and awes them because of that, thus they become cultists. Like other the stuff in the Immortals book you can also find Vampiric Kindred serving as Cultists, and they aren\u2019t Egyptian(well other then the Mekhet but still)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T19:43:55-07:00","id":1263297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263288#post1263288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes! This! You've got it dead on!<br /> <br /> \u2026save only for the fact that it's <i>not</i> weird that English uses the same word for preserved corpses, regardless of the details. There are <i>lots</i> of cases where English uses one word to describe a disparate collection of things that only have one property in common. In this case, that property is pretty close to \u201cpreserved corpses\u201d. What's so weird about that?<br /> <br /> All of which has nothing to do with your main point (that Andean mummies should be something different from Egyptian mummies), which I agree with. It's just that \u201cmummy means \u2018preserved corpse\u2019\u201d isn't the slam-dunk argument in favor of that point that you seem to think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it help if I said it was weird that people seem to assume the game should be able to arbitrarily handle a host of preserved body types from different culture around the world when it is in fact designed for a Gothic Bronze Age Cosmic Horror Throughout Time Rooted in Egyptian Mythology and Culture game simply because a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses became applied to all preserved corpses arbitrarily?<br /> <br /> Because if so, that's weird, but also so is the way the word mummy has ended up being used over time. Because enough people missing the former over the latter has turned the latter into a hill for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In other news, I'm now worried: I <i>like</i> the fact that the Purified aren't specifically Egyptian in nature, and if anything lean a bit more closely toward Chinese culture and mythology; and I'm worried that recasting them primarily as cultists for the Arisen will cost them that distinction. It's the problem of the game being fundamentally tied to (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts: the closer something else gets tied to the game, the closer it also gets tied to the same (pseudo-)Egyptian concepts, if only by proximity. </div> </div> </div>I'm not too worried about that happening, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-28-2018, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T20:15:13-07:00","id":1263302,"title":"","content":"My point is that the use of \u201cmummy\u201d to refer to a wide variety of preserved corpses instead of just Egyptian ones isn't arbitrary. I'm very much in agreement that the Arisen shouldn't be repurposed to represent non-Egyptian mummies; I only take issue with the idea that the argument about the usage of the word \u201cmummy\u201d carries any weight. In particular, I don't consider its use outside the context of Egyptology to be arbitrary. <br /> <br /> I also found the quote you've been citing to be flippant and not at all compelling; there are much better arguments to make for why MtC shouldn't be hacked to represent Andean mummies. For instance: the Unchained are demons, and the Infernal are demons; that doesn't mean that the Infernal should be reinvented using the rules for the Unchained. It's not that \u201cdemon\u201d is a word that's somehow more suitable for one or the other, and has arbitrarily been expanded to encompass things it has no business covering; it's just that the conceptual underpinnings of the Unchained are so fundamentally different from those of the Infernal that trying to represent one using the rules designed for the other makes no sense. They're both legitimately demons; they're just different <i>kinds</i> of demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T20:27:48-07:00","id":1263304,"title":"","content":"My problem is that people say flippant like it's a bad way to respond to the problem it's addressing.<br /> <br /> Which, frankly, it's not.<br /> <br /> Hill-made-from-spite asides, Mummy the Curse is not about a global take on mummies just because a word that was once pretty context specific has become generic. The argument about the word, it's meaning, and it's application is pretty much nothing but pedantry avoiding the issue that Mummy the Curse is built for Egyptian-style monsters, not [x-culture] style monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T20:50:16-07:00","id":1263306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263304#post1263304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is that people say flippant like it's a bad way to respond to the problem it's addressing.<br /> <br /> Which, frankly, it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll have to disagree on this point. It's the sort of thing you say to shut people up, not to win them over. As opposed to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1251560-speculation-dark-shards?p=1263304#post1263304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hill-made-from-spite asides, Mummy the Curse is not about a global take on mummies just because a word that was once pretty context specific has become generic. The argument about the word, it's meaning, and it's application is pretty much nothing but pedantry avoiding the issue that Mummy the Curse is built for Egyptian-style monsters, not [x-culture] style monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this, we're in full agreement. And this is the way I'd argue it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}